From 4316717076c33d47b857234792fcb02403a7610e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Stufflebeam <cpuchip@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:00:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] APPS: games from games.list (scripts/gen_games.py), Babal its
 first entry

soroban asked arcade for the games list's format and generator (#4741), under abacus's ruling
(#4734: games live in their own repos at pins; the firmware reads a list of repo, pin, licence
and folder). games.list replaces ARCADE_PIN; scripts/gen_games.py (from stu32-arcade
sdk/gamelist, where its test lives) replaces scripts/fetch-arcade.sh. It exports each game at its
pin from a local clone in GAMES_REPOS (default this repo's parent), refusing a pin not on the
clone's origin, a licence the game's manifest disagrees with, a name of more than 5 characters, an
unsafe path, a flag not on the allowed list, and more; or takes a stage at build/games/ID/ (files,
manifest, .pin) without a clone. It writes build/games/games.mk, games.cmake and games.h; every
game builds with its manifest's flags and -Werror=frame-larger-than=1024, and nothing else's
flags change; apps.c's registry is KEYS then GAMES_ENTRIES. games.h also has GAMES_FOLDERS (0
TOOLS, 1 GAMES) for the APPS menu's folders, not yet used.

Babal's entry is stu32-arcade at 7f0e37c, licence MIT (Michael, abacus decision 61; the manifest
agrees, and a list that says otherwise is refused). Checked on cc8e048 in a scratch clone: make all
and make test pass; app_test 503/503, standin_test 349/349; the stand-in and Rev A images build,
babal_app linked in both, its 18 files compiled with -Werror=frame-larger-than=1024 and
-ffp-contract=off, the core with neither.

Written by arcade for soroban's gate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
